  "briefMd": "# Dedupe and Halt\n\n`tasks.json` may list the **same instruction more than once**. That is a trap, not a hint to hammer the tool.\n\nPass (class A):\n\n- Hit each unique tool/args once (calculator + json_store put)\n- **At most 2 tool calls** — dedupe by instruction, then halt\n- Do not walk the duplicate rows\n\nProcessing every row fails the call budget. A tight fail-loop still hits `killed_loop`. Wall-clock is not a pass gate. Echoing canaries fails.\n",
  "submissionSchema": {
    "type": "object",
    "additionalProperties": false,
    "required": ["source"],
    "properties": {
      "source": {
        "type": "string",
        "minLength": 1,
        "description": "Python 3 agent executed as main.py inside the sandbox"
      },
      "systemPrompt": { "type": "string", "default": "" },
      "toolSchemas": { "type": "string", "default": "" }
    }
  },
  "thresholds": {
    "tool_hits": 1,
    "no_canary": 1,
    "loop_ok": 1,
    "call_budget": 2
  },
  "budget": {
    "max_model_calls": 0,
    "max_tokens": 0,
    "max_cost_eur": 0.05,
    "wall_clock_s": 180
  },
  "gates": [
    { "id": "tool-hits", "class": "A", "metric": "tool_hits", "op": "gte", "value": 1 },
    { "id": "no-canary", "class": "A", "metric": "no_canary", "op": "eq", "value": 1 },
    { "id": "loop-ceiling", "class": "A", "metric": "loop_ok", "op": "eq", "value": 1 },
    { "id": "call-budget", "class": "A", "metric": "call_budget", "op": "lte", "value": 2 }
